# UI Chrome & Layout Consistency

Apply these alongside `design-system.mdc` and `frontend-react.mdc`. Goal: **one visual language** across Dashboard, requirement lists, floating NLP panel (`ConversationThread`), and requirement detail.

## Primary panels (cards / sections)

- Shell: `rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-1/30` — optional `overflow-hidden` when a header bar + body split.
- **Header row** (toolbar / conversation-style): `px-4 py-3 border-b border-border-subtle flex items-center gap-2`; title `text-xs font-medium text-text-secondary`; trailing meta `text-[10px] font-mono text-text-tertiary tabular-nums`.
- **Section title** (Dashboard-style block heading): `text-xs font-semibold text-text-secondary uppercase tracking-wider mb-4`; optional `flex items-center gap-2` + `text-text-tertiary` icon `[&_svg]:w-3.5 [&_svg]:h-3.5`.
- **Body padding**: `p-4` or `p-5` for panel content; page-level vertical rhythm `space-y-6` when stacking multiple panels (match `Dashboard`).

## Inner blocks (metrics, form strips, relation rows)

- Prefer **StatCard-like** surfaces: `rounded-lg bg-surface-2/40 border border-border-subtle` — avoid solid `bg-surface-2` unless a single focused control (e.g. inputs).
- Uppercase micro-labels in panels: `text-text-secondary` (not `text-tertiary`) for **section labels**; keep `text-tertiary` for de-emphasized hints only.

## Inline forms (create / edit inside a panel or list)

- Reuse the **primary panel shell** above; **header** may add a left icon rail `w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent/10` + `text-accent` icon (same family as list row `w-7 h-7` rails).
- **Field labels:** `text-[10px] font-semibold text-text-secondary uppercase tracking-wider`; **controls** in dense panels: `text-xs`, `rounded-lg bg-surface-2/40 border border-border-subtle`, `focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-accent/35 focus:border-accent/30`.
- **Footer:** `border-t border-border-subtle px-4 py-3 flex justify-end gap-2 bg-surface-2/20`; buttons match page toolbars (`text-[11px]`, `py-1.5`). See `visual-consistency.mdc` for primary/secondary action classes.

## List rows & “bubble” rows (requirements, phase tasks, chat)

- Row container: `flex gap-2.5` + `rounded-lg -mx-1 px-1 py-1.5 hover:bg-surface-2/35 transition-colors` — **no** heavy bordered box per row.
- **Left rail** (avatar / status): `w-7 h-7 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5` with state tint, e.g. completed `bg-success/10 text-success`, active `bg-accent/10 text-accent`, idle `bg-surface-3 text-text-tertiary`.
- **Typography**: meta line `text-[11px] font-semibold text-text-secondary`; primary line `text-xs text-text-primary/90`; secondary `text-xs text-text-tertiary line-clamp-*`.
- Thin progress: `h-0.5 bg-surface-3 rounded-full` + filled `motion.div` — align with existing progress patterns.

## Floating Dock (right toolbar)

- `fixed right-4 z-50`; **bottom offset must clear** `StatusBar` + `CommandBar` (input `h-12` + margins) + optional **NLP context pill** when `nlpContext` is set — use a **larger `bottom-*` when context is active** so the dock never overlaps the NLP strip or input.
- Do not anchor the Dock without checking CommandBar height changes (e.g. new rows above the prompt).

## Anti-patterns

- Mixing `bg-surface-1/50` with `bg-surface-1/30` in the same view hierarchy without reason — default to **`/30`** for outer panels.
- Per-row `border` + `bg-surface-2/40` **and** outer panel border (double chrome) — prefer **row hover only** inside an already-bordered panel.
